          "fact": "The diamond play and club development route are feasible.",
          "explanation": "North holds D3, South holds DA and DK, and CA-CK followed by a club to North's CQ is available with AK864 opposite Q72. Side entries remain in hearts, diamonds and spades; the plan appropriately allows reassessment of unknown club breaks.",
          "quotes": [
            "Follow with the lowest diamond, preserving dummy's higher spot cards; South can take the trick with DA.",
            "cash CA and CK, then continue clubs to establish the suit, using dummy's CQ as an entry if needed."
          ]
